    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<div class=\"rd__b  rd__b--1\"><div class=\"rd__b  rd__b--2\"><p><strong>火矮人Azer</strong></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:left;MARGIN:0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\">“我只要一百個火矮人奴隸，就可以建起一個讓衆神也爲之動容的帝國。”</em></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:right;MARGIN:0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan;text-align:right\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\">火巨靈帕沙，阿克瑟斯?奧賽誇 Arakses al-Saqar</em></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:left;MARGIN:0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan\"></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:left;MARGIN:0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan\">火矮人是火元素位面的原住民，它們是工藝大師、採礦專家，還是火巨靈efreet的誓敵。火矮人的外觀和舉止類似男性矮人，不過這只是假象。其烈焰般的頭髮和鬍鬚，正好彰顯其金屬皮膚下全由火焰構成的本質。</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:left;MARGIN:0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><strong>鑄成的生命Made, Not Born。</strong></em>火矮人不能生育。它們的身軀由另一個火矮人用青銅鑄成，再由鑄造者注入一份它的生命之火。每個火矮人都被雕刻成獨特的外觀。鑄造的過程限制了人口的增長速度，因此火矮人相當稀少。</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:left;MARGIN:0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><strong>火山居民Volcanic Dwellers。</strong></em>火矮人居住在火元素位面與土元素位面交界處一個火山林立的國度。火矮人們活動於層巒疊嶂下的火山口與岩漿戶裏，從中開採着閃耀的金屬和寶石。火矮人小分隊在隘口和地道間巡邏，抵禦着火巨靈派來入侵國度的火蜥蜴掠奪者salamander raiders。</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:left;MARGIN:0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><strong>火巨靈之敵Enemies of the Efreet。</strong></em>很久以前，火巨靈與火矮人曾是盟友。火矮人們還協助建造了火巨靈的家園黃銅之城City of Brass，並將其打造成世上最令人驚歎的奇觀之一。然而在火矮人完工之際，火巨靈卻背叛了盟友，甚至意圖奴役火矮人以爲防止城市的機密外泄。雖然火巨靈的奴役計劃最終失敗，但雙方至今仍只是偶爾的劫掠和小規模衝突，並沒有爆發全面的戰爭。火矮人們認爲火巨靈是擔心它們會公開進入黃銅之城的祕密通道，因而纔不敢輕舉妄動。</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:left;MARGIN:0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><strong>金屬與寶石大師Master of Metal and Fems。</strong></em>火矮人是工藝大師，能將火山中開採出的寶石和稀有金屬鑄造成美麗的工藝品。在它們認爲這些珍寶的價值超越一切，並且時常派遣團隊跨越位面前去尋找珍稀的金屬和寶石。當火矮人被魔法召喚到主物質位面時，通常都是爲了協助鑄造精巧的魔法物品或藝術品。據說火矮人的技藝天下無雙。</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:left;MARGIN:0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><strong>活體火焰Living Fire。</strong></em>火矮人無需食物、飲水、睡眠。</p><p>Natives of the Elemental Plane of Fire, azers are master crafters, expert miners, and sworn foes of the efreet. In appearance and manner, an azer resembles a male dwarf, but this is a facade. Beneath its metallic looking skin, an azer is a being of fire, which outwardly manifests in its fiery hair and beard.</p><div data-roll-name-ancestor=\"Made, Not Born\" class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p><span class=\"entry-title-inner\">Made, Not Born.</span> Azers don't reproduce. They are each crafted from bronze by another azer and imbued with a portion of the crafter's inner flame. Each azer is sculpted with unique features. This crafting process limits the growth of the azer population and is the primary reason that these creatures remain rare.</p></div><div data-roll-name-ancestor=\"Volcanic Dwellers\" class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p><span class=\"entry-title-inner\">Volcanic Dwellers.</span> Azers dwell in a kingdom on the border between the Elemental Plane of Earth and the Elemental Plane of Fire-a range of mountains and volcanoes whose spires rise as a series of fortresses. Beneath mountain peaks, under volcanic calderas, and amid rivers of magma, azers extract gleaming metals and glittering gems from the earth. Squads of azer patrol the passes and tunnels of their realm, fending off the salamander raiders whose efreet masters order strikes against the azer kingdom.</p></div><div data-roll-name-ancestor=\"Enemies of the Efreet\" class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p><span class=\"entry-title-inner\">Enemies of the Efreet.</span> Long ago, the efreet and the azers were allies. Azers helped create the City of Brass, forging that home of the efreet into one of the most wondrous places in creation. When the azers had finished their work, the efreet betrayed them, making a failed attempt to enslave the azers so as to protect the secrets of the city. Despite occasional raids and skirmishes, however, the two sides have so far refrained from all-out conflict. The azers believe that only the threat of them revealing the hidden ways into the City of Brass keeps the efreet in check.</p></div><div data-roll-name-ancestor=\"Masters of Metal and Gems\" class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p><span class=\"entry-title-inner\">Masters of Metal and Gems.</span> Azers are masterful artisans, and create beautiful works from the gems and precious metals found in their volcanic habitat. They rate the value of such treasures above all other things, sometimes dispatching parties across the planes to seek out rare metals and gemstones.</p><p>When azers are called by magic to the Material Plane, it is typically to help forge an elaborate magic item or work of art, for it is said that their skill in such craft knows no equal.</p></div><div data-roll-name-ancestor=\"Living Fire\" class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p><span class=\"entry-title-inner\">Living Fire.</span> An azer doesn't require food, drink, or sleep.</p></div></div><div class=\"rd__b-special rd__b-inset rd__b-inset--readaloud\"><div class=\"rd__quote\"><p class=\"rd__quote-line rd__quote-line--last\">“<em>Give me a hundred azer slaves, and I can forge an empire that would make the gods tremble.</em>”</p><p><span class=\"rd__quote-by\">— Arakses al-Saqar, efreeti pasha</span></p></div></div></div>",
        "public": ""
      },
